The argument claims the displayed relation is a nontrivial linear combination, which requires some coefficient $ s{t}_j\mm s{z}_{j,k_h}$ to be nonzero. The example only ensures $ s{p}_j\mm s{z}_{j,k_h}
e s{0}$, and in a tubal ring (which has zero divisors) $ s{t}_j\mm s{z}= s{0}$ can coexist with $ s{p}_j\mm s{z}= s{z}
e s{0}$ -- e.g. any $ s{z}\in\dotp{ s{p}_j}$ satisfies $ s{t}_j\mm s{z}= s{0}$ while $ s{p}_j\mm s{z}= s{z}
e s{0}$. Hence the displayed relation may be trivial and the printed argument does not establish that $\operatorname{Image}(T_{	X})$ is not a free module. (The conclusion is in fact true -- it follows from the nested supports of the singular tubes forced by the coordinatewise ordering in \Cref{thm:tSVDM} -- but the printed argument does not prove it.)
